DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The VVFFSS__VVGGEETT() looks up or creates a vnode from a (mount, inode#) tuple.

     Its arguments are:

     _m_p     The mount point.

     _i_n_o    The inode representing the file.  This is a unique number assigned
            by the file system when vnodes are first created.

     _f_l_a_g_s  Additional locking flags to pass through to vget(9).

     _v_p_p    Return parameter for the vnode.

     This is an optional file system entry-point for file systems mainly in‐
     tended for NFS server use, but many file systems use it internally in
     VOP_LOOKUP(9) and similar.

     If the file system does not support this call, then it should return
     EOPNOTSUPP.

